133:     - "Run upstream_assets.codex_agents with --check. Covers the generated .codex/agents/*.toml. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift."
134:     - "Run upstream_assets.codex_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .codex/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift."
135:     - "Run upstream_assets.agent_roster. Covers roster coverage across all five surfaces and rejects a real file where a symlink belongs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error (bad argument, canonical dir missing, or crash)."
136:     - "Run upstream_assets.command_catalog. Compare command frontmatter with the root and family indexes and hub metadata. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error."
137:     - "Run upstream_assets.codex_hooks_installer with --check --allow-worktree. Covers the user-global ~/.codex/hooks.json against the repo's .codex/hooks.json, including orphaned entries whose .skilled adapter no longer exists on disk. Explicit OK output = in sync; a drift report = drift; refusal, error, or missing affirmative output = error."
138:     - "Run upstream_assets.pi_agents with --check. Covers the generated .pi/agents/*.md. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift."
139:     - "Run upstream_assets.pi_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .pi/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift."
140:     - "For each row in hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks, run its file_exists check (a plain path-existence read, no execution of the adapter or the shell command that wraps it). Collect every row whose path does not resolve as a degraded hook adapter, keyed by host:event:path."
141:     - "Aggregate: report each surface with its own verdict rather than a single pass/fail, so the operator learns which mirror moved."
142: 
