144: # OUTPUT
145: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
146: output: |
147:   STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync.
148:   STATUS=DRIFT when any checker reports drift, listing each drifting surface and the repair command for it:
149:     runtime mirrors  -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs
150:     codex agents     -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs
151:     codex prompts    -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs
152:     codex hooks      -> node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs
153:     pi agents        -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs
154:     pi prompts       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs
155:     command catalog  -> update the root and family indexes, group counts, and hub metadata from command frontmatter
156:   The agent roster check has no generator; its drift is repaired by the runtime-mirrors generator or by hand
157:   for the authored surfaces (.skilled/agents, .codex/agents).
158:   Hook CONFIG STRUCTURE is deliberately out of scope for mirroring: the four runtimes use incompatible event
159:   vocabularies and entry shapes, so those files are hand-authored per runtime and cannot be mirror-checked
160:   against each other.
161:   Separately, "N hook adapters degraded to fallback" reports the count of hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks
162:   rows whose path does not resolve, each listed as host:event:path. This is the same drift a live adapter
163:   failure produces (its fallback JSON would carry "mkHookDrift": true and its stderr a matching
164:   "mk-hook-drift host=<host> event=<event> adapter=<name>" line) surfaced without needing to fire the hook or
165:   read raw JSON. Repair is adapter-specific: rebuild the runtime (npm --prefix
166:   .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build) for a dist/hooks/* path, or restore/recreate the named
167:   script for a .skilled/bin or .skilled/hooks path.
168:   STATUS=ERROR when a checker refuses to run, returns an error, or omits an affirmative result.

